#N canvas 0 0 760 760 10;
#X text 12 8 nes~ - RP2A03 (NES APU): 2 pulses + triangle + noise + DPCM;
#X text 12 28 The playback/generation split follows vgm~ + opl3~: raw register writes (`nes <reg 0-31> <val>` = VGM 0xBC bytes \, `reg` is the alias) or the voice layer. A message is a COMMAND STREAM - every word is a command consuming its own args \, so `note 60 100 duty 2` runs both in one message (comma forms still fine). `chN` (N = 1..5) scopes the rest of THAT message to channel N - it never keys off another channel and the gate inlet stays ch1. Voice notes drive constant volume (vel 0-127 -> volume register 0-15)\; vel 0 = key off (the 2A03 has no release stage);
#X text 12 118 outlets (signal): 0 = the chip's own mix (the nesdev non-linear DAC equation) \, 1..5 = pulse 1 / pulse 2 / triangle / noise / DPCM alone (bipolarized \, +-0.25 each\; noise uses the live LFSR orbit's density and fades its gate 3 ms \, DPCM is AC-coupled - a held DAC level fades out instead of clicking at enable boundaries). NO clip - attenuate before dac~;
#X msg 20 330 reset \, note 60 100;
#X text 200 330 ch1 pulse: A4 \, vel 100 -> volume 12;
#X msg 20 360 note 64 90 duty 1;
#X text 200 360 chained stream: re-key + duty 25%;
#X msg 20 390 ch2 note 65 80;
#X text 200 390 ch2 harmony (ch1 keeps sounding);
#X msg 20 420 ch3 note 48 100;
#X text 200 420 ch3 triangle bass;
#X msg 20 450 ch4 note 60 100 mode 1;
#X text 200 450 ch4 noise: short LFSR \, pitch -> period idx;
#X msg 20 480 ch1 gate 0;
#X text 200 480 per-channel release;
#X msg 20 510 ch2 gate 0 \, ch3 gate 0 \, ch4 gate 0;
#X text 200 510 release the rest;
#X msg 400 330 nes 15 1;
#X text 560 330 raw: enable pulse 1 ($4015);
#X msg 400 360 nes 0 191;
#X text 560 360 raw: $4000 = 191 (duty 2 \, halt+constant \, vol 15) - pd message boxes parse decimal only \, never hex;
#X msg 400 390 nes 2 253 \, nes 3 8;
#X text 560 390 raw: $4002 = 253 (A4) + $4003 = 8 (length load);
#X msg 400 420 nes 15 0;
#X text 560 420 raw: everything off;
#X msg 400 450 status;
#X text 560 450 per-channel state dump to the console;
#X msg 400 480 clock 1662607;
#X text 560 480 PAL CPU clock (swaps rate tables);
#X msg 400 510 clock 1789773;
#X text 560 510 back to NTSC;
#X msg 400 540 reset;
#X text 560 540 power-on state (silent);
#X obj 20 580 nes~;
#X obj 20 640 *~ 0.5;
#X obj 20 680 dac~;
#X text 20 720 in a VGM patch: vgm~ outlet 1 -> nes~ inlet (see nes-player.pd). Sibling selectors psg/gg/ay/opl are dropped silently;
